# Re-evaluate & De-stale the AH Comment on EVERY Field-State Change — MANDATORY

The AH review-comment column (**AH**, header `GDC AI Tool Comments`) is a
per-field running record. A note that was true at one point becomes a LIE the
moment the field's reality changes. Therefore, whenever ANYTHING about a field
changes, you MUST re-read that field's AH cell LIVE, compare it to the new
reality, and fix any note that is now stale, inaccurate, or contradicted. A
field operation is NOT "done" while its AH cell still says something untrue.

## Why this rule exists (real incident, 2026-09-09)

On `TI_Fnt_ExportImportRelatedInfo__c`, 10 formula fields carried a
`[FIX 2026-09-08]` AH note saying *"formula body on the sheet was a JP
placeholder/description … replaced with dummy \"TBD\""*. That note was written
while the pipeline was reading the WRONG column (G). After the column fix (read
col H), the sheet actually held a REAL formula — so the old note was now false
and misleading. The comment had to be re-evaluated and superseded with an
accurate `[VALIDATION 2026-09-09]` note. Had we skipped the re-evaluation, the
sheet would have carried a wrong explanation of each field's state.

## When this fires (every time — no exceptions)

Re-evaluate the AH comment for a field whenever ANY of the following happens:

- The field is **(re)deployed** (create OR update — formula body, picklist
  values, length, precision/scale, referenceTo, type, required, etc.).
- The field is **delete+recreated** (data-type change) or **destructively
  deleted** (IsDelete).
- The field is **parked / flagged as a blocker** (or a prior blocker is
  RESOLVED — the "blocked" note must then be cleared/updated).
- The field's **sheet definition or any attribute is edited** (incl. an
  attribute write-back per `sf-deploy-delta-and-blockers.mdc`), or a
  drift/attribute-fix is applied.
- A **tool/reader change** (e.g. the col-G→col-H fix) changes what the sheet was
  understood to say for that field.
- You are doing the mandatory "review comments for all deployed fields" pass.

## Required behavior

1. **Read the field's AH cell LIVE** (per `read-sheet-live.mdc`) right before/
   after the change — never judge staleness from memory or a cached snapshot.
2. **Compare every existing AH note to the new reality.** A note is STALE if it
   states a cause, value, or status that the current org/sheet no longer bears
   (e.g. "replaced with dummy" when the real value is now deployed; "blocked:
   target missing" after the target was added and the field deployed; a picklist
   value set that no longer matches; a formula body that changed).
3. **Correct stale notes — do not just pile on.** AH is append-only by tool
   default (`write_ai_comments.py` APPENDS + de-dupes), so the DEFAULT correction
   is to append a dated superseding note (`[VALIDATION <date>]` / `[FIX <date>]`)
   that states the current truth and, when useful, explicitly says it supersedes
   the earlier note. When an old note is outright FALSE and appending would
   confuse the reader, OVERWRITE that cell instead — but only with the user's
   confirmation (it is still a gated write), and preserve any still-valid history.
4. **Keep AH and AI consistent.** The AH note's stated status must agree with the
   AI `Deployment Status` value set per `sf-deploy-status-column-always.mdc`
   (e.g. don't leave AH saying "not deployed" while AI says `Deployed`).
5. **Gated write.** Every AH edit (append OR overwrite) is a gated sheet write
   (`sheet-write-confirmation.mdc`): preview the `cell: old → new` diff and get
   confirmation before `--apply`. Prefer `flag_blocker.py` for blocker notes
   (coupled AH note + Col-A highlight) and `write_ai_comments.py` for fix/
   validation notes.

## Guardrails

- No field change is complete until its AH comment has been re-evaluated and any
  stale note corrected — this is as mandatory as the AI status update.
- Never delete genuine history gratuitously; supersede by default, overwrite only
  when a note is actively misleading and the user approves.
- All AH reads are LIVE and header-driven (`GDC AI Tool Comments`, fallback
  `FreeColumnGDC1` / index 33); WIP rows are skipped.
